Smoot maintainers have discussed merging Signare library to Smoot project. This signing service could be very useful for multisign signing using HSM.  The package needs bug issues and capability expensions.

Signare, a Hyperledger Lab, is an enterprise grade digital signing solution for DLT related applications and Ethereum clients. The application provides a REST API server to manage resource configuration and an ETH-JSON-RPC 2.0 server that provides functionality for generating, removing, listing and signing Ethereum transactions.

There are two ways for governance to port the Signare repo:
  Option 1: Simply create an empty signare repo under LFDT-Smoot.  The maintainers will do the rest.
  Option 2: Fork only the main branch of https://github.com/hyperledger-labs/signare.
